          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ExamplesSchroedingerRepresentation Schrödinger representation
          %p
            We discuss how the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+representation"} Schrödinger representation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+commutation+relation"} canonical commutation relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{q,p\} = -1
            arises via geometric quantization:
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            with canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
            denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{q,p\}
            and to be called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinate"} canonical coordinate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momentum"} canonical momentum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+form"} constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
            given in in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CanonicalMomentumPresymplecticCurrent"} (?)
            by
          #eq:R2SymplecticForm.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega = d p \wedge d q
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+differential+form"} closed
            in that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \omega = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector+fields"} tangent vector fields
            into it (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractionOfFormsWithVectorFields"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-forms"} differential 1-forms
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
          %p
            A choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+potential"} presymplectic potential
            for this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            is
          #eq:CanonicalSymplecticPotentialOnR2.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta \;\coloneqq\; - q \, d p
          %p
            in that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi θ
                    %mo =
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \theta = \omega
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta = p \, d q
          %p For
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^2
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{C}
          %p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            (an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
            for it (as in def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HamiltonianForms"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector+field"} tangent vector field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_A
            whose contraction into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:R2SymplecticForm"} (2)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          #eq:HamiltonianVectorFieldOnR2.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi A
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_{v_A} \omega = d A
                  \\,.
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
            of this phase space by constant-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            \-slices
          #eq:ConstantqSlicesOnR2.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda_q = \subset \mathbb{R}^2
                  \\,.
          %p
            These are also called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
            of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+polarization"} real polarization
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
          %p
            (Other choices of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            are possible, notably the constant
            = succeed "-slices.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p We says that a smooth function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^2 \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
          %p
            is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarized
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \theta
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
            vanishes; which for the choice of polarization in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConstantqSlicesOnR2"} (5)
            means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi p
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi p
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi d
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi θ
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla_{\partial_p} \psi = 0
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\iota_{\partial_p} \left(  d \psi + i \theta \psi \right)
                  \=
                  0
                  \\,,
          %p
            which in turn, for the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+potential"} presymplectic potential
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CanonicalSymplecticPotentialOnR2"} (3)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mo ∂
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi p
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo −
                  %mi i
                  %mi q
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{\partial}{\partial p} \psi - i q \psi = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            The solutions to this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            are of the form
          #eq:PolarizedFunctionsForBasicExampleOnR2.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mi i
                  %mi p
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi(q,p) = \psi(q) \, \exp(+ i p q)
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{C}
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
          %p
            This establishes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+isomorphism"} linear isomorphism
            between polarized smooth functions and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+functions"} wave functions
          %p
            By
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HamiltonianVectorFieldOnR2"} (4)
            we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAAA
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  v_q = \partial_p
                  \\phantom{AAAA}
                  v_p = -\partial_q
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            is
          #eq:R2PoissonBracket.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi v
                                %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi v
                                %mi q
                          %mi ω
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi q
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi p
                          %mi d
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi d
                          %mi q
                          %mo =
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\{q,p\}
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\iota_{v_p} \iota_{v_q}  \omega
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \-\iota_{\partial_q} \iota_{\partial_p} d p \wedge d q
                  \=
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \- 1
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            The action of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+operator+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} quantum operators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat q
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat p
            on the polarized functions
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PolarizedFunctionsForBasicExampleOnR2"} (6)
            is as follows
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mo ∇
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi p
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi i
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %munder
                                  %munder
                                    %mrow
                                      %mfrac
                                        %mo ∂
                                        %mrow
                                          %mo ∂
                                          %mi p
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo (
                                        %mi ψ
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                        %mi q
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                        %msup
                                          %mi e
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi i
                                            %mi q
                                            %mi p
                                        %mo )
                                    %mo ⏟
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo =
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi q
                                    %mi Ψ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi q
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                                %mi q
                                %mi Ψ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi q
                                %mo ,
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi q
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi q
                              %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\hat q \Psi(q,p)
                  \&amp; =
                  \- i \nabla_{\partial_p}\Psi(q,p) + q \Psi(q,p)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = -i
                  \\underset{ = 0 }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\left(
                  \\underset{
                  \= i q \Psi(q,p)
                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\frac{\partial}{\partial p}
                  \\left(
                  \\psi(q) e^{i q p}
                  \\right)
                  }
                  }
                  \- i q \Psi(q,p)
                  \\right)
                  }
                  }
                  +
                  q \Psi(q,p)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \left( q \psi(q) \right) e^{i q p}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mo ∇
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi q
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi p
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi i
                          %mfrac
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi q
                              %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi p
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi i
                            %mfrac
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi q
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi q
                              %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %munder
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi ψ
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi q
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo (
                                        %mi i
                                        %mfrac
                                          %mo ∂
                                          %mrow
                                            %mo ∂
                                            %mi q
                                        %msup
                                          %mi e
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi i
                                            %mi q
                                            %mi p
                                        %mo )
                                    %mo ⏟
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo =
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi Ψ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi q
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo +
                                %mi p
                                %mi Ψ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi q
                                %mo ,
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi i
                            %mfrac
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi q
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi p
                              %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\hat p \Psi(q,p)
                  \&amp; =
                  i \nabla_{\partial_q} \Psi(q,p) + p \Psi(q,p)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = i \frac{\partial}{\partial q} (\psi(q)e^{i q p}) + p \Psi(q,p)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\left(
                  i \frac{\partial}{\partial q}\psi(q)
                  \\right) e^{i q p}
                  +
                  \\underset{ = 0}{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\underset{
                  \= - p \Psi(q,p)
                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\psi(q)
                  \\left(
                  i \frac{\partial}{\partial q} e^{i q p}
                  \\right)
                  }
                  }
                  +
                  p \Psi(q,p)
                  }
                  }
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\left(
                  i \frac{\partial}{\partial q}\psi(q)
                  \\right) e^{i p q}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence under the identification
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PolarizedFunctionsForBasicExampleOnR2"} (6)
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mi q
                  %mi ψ
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAAA
                  %mover
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                  %mfrac
                    %mo ∂
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi q
                  %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat q \psi = q \psi
                  \\phantom{AAAA}
                  \\hat p \psi = i \frac{\partial}{\partial q} \psi
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+representation"} Schrödinger representation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+commutation+relation"} canonical commutation relation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:R2PoissonBracket"} (7)
          %h3#khler_manifolds Kähler manifolds
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \omega)
            happens to be also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} Kähler manifold
            there are natural choices of prequantization:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
                since its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msubsup
                          %mi T
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in T^*_{(1,1)}X
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
                is given by the anti-holomorphic tangent bundle
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{0,1}X
            %li
              %p
                a polarized section is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+section"} holomorphic section
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} space of states (in geometric quantization)
                is given by the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann-Roch+theorem"} Riemann-Roch theorem
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Hitchin"} Hitchin
          %p
            Applied to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            this yields the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Bargmann-Fock representation
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bargmann-Fock+representation"} ?
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
          %h3#ExampleThe2Sphere The 2-sphere
          %p
            Consider the 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            with its canonical round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            which preserves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+metric"} Kähler metric
            is a multiple of the standard round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on the 2-sphere.
          %p
            By the identification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1) \simeq K(\mathbb{Z},2)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundles"} prequantum bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            are classified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
