                  \\,,
          %p
            the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+sections"} holomorphic sections
            of such a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            naturally acts on this Hilbert space. The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate"} coordinate
            functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
