                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+Kirillov"}> Alexandre Kirillov
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dynamical systems IV
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-06793-2_2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-06793-2_2
            %li#Woodhouse
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Woodhouse"}> Nicholas Woodhouse
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Quantization
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/geometric-quantization-9780198502708"} ISBN:9780198502708
          %p Introductions and lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                William Gordon Ritter,
                %em Geometric Quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0208008"}> arXiv:math-ph/0208008
                )
            %li#Blau
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Blau"}> Matthias Blau
                ,
                %em Symplectic geometry and geometric quantization
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BlauGeometricQuantization.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Lerman
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugene+Lerman"}> Eugene Lerman
                ,
                %em Geometric quantization; a crash course
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2334"}> arXiv:1206.2334
                )
            %li
              %p
                Andrea Carosso:
                %em Geometric Quantization
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.02307"}> arXiv:1801.02307
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Kadri İlker Berktav, Burak Oğuz, Ömer Önder, Yunus Emre Sargut, Başar Deniz Sevinç, Deniz Nazif Taştan:
                %em A Mathematical Introduction to Geometric Quantization
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.03171"}> arXiv:2512.03171
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Lecture notes with an emphasis on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiclassical+states"} semiclassical states
          %ul
            %li#BatesWeinstein
              Sean Bates,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+the+geometry+of+quantization"} Lectures on the geometry of quantization
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.berkeley.edu/~alanw/GofQ.pdf"} pdf
          %p A careful discussion of the polarization-step from prequantization to quantization is in
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Śniatycki75"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C4%99drzej+%C5%9Aniatycki"}> Jędrzej Śniatycki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wave functions relative to a real polarization
                %strong 14
                4 (1975) 277-288 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01807689"}> doi:10.1007/BF01807689)
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li{:id => "Śniatycki80"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C4%99drzej+%C5%9Aniatycki"}> Jędrzej Śniatycki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Quantization and Quantum Mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 30
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-6066-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-6066-0
            %li{:id => "Śniatycki16"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C4%99drzej+%C5%9Aniatycki"}> Jędrzej Śniatycki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Geometric Quantization
                %em Geom. Integrability &amp; Quantization
                (2016) 95-129 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/ebooks/geometry-integrability-and-quantization-proceedings-series/Lectures-on-Geometric-Quantization/chapter/Lectures-on-Geometric-Quantization/10.7546/giq-17-2016-95-129"}> doi:10.7546/giq-17-2016-95-129
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The special case of Kähler quantization is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Hitchin
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> Nigel Hitchin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
              %strong 131
              (1990), no. 2, 347–380.
          %p and for almost Kähler structure in
          %ul
            %li#BorthwickUribe96
              David Borthwick, Alejandro Uribe,
              %em Almost complex structures and geometric quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9608006"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9608006
              )
          %p
            Discussion with an emphasis of quantizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
            on curved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Woodhouse"}> Nicholas Woodhouse
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization and quantum field theory in curved space-times
              %strong 12
              1 (1977) 45-56 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0034-4877(77)90045-3"}> doi:10.1016/0034-4877(77)90045-3
              ]
          %p
            (For more on geometric quantization of quantum field theories see also at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "multisymplectic+geometry#RefsonQuantization"} Quantization of multisymplectic geometry
          %p Aspects at least of geometric prequantization are usefully discussed also in section II of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780817647308"} doi:10.1007/978-0-8176-4731-5
          %p Further reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A. Echeverria-Enriquez, M.C. Munoz-Lecanda, N. Roman-Roy, C. Victoria-Monge,
                %em Mathematical Foundations of Geometric Quantization
                Extracta Math. 13 (1998) 135-238 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/9904008"}> arXiv:math-ph/9904008
                )
            %li
              %p
                Nima Moshayedi,
                %em Notes on Geometric Quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.15419"}> arXiv:2010.15419
                )
          %p The above “Overview” and “Basic Jargon” sections are taken from
          %ul
            %li#Baez
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %em Geometric Quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/quantization.html"}> web
              )
          %p Some useful talk notes include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eva+Miranda"}> Eva Miranda
              \:
              %em From action-angle coordinates to geometric quantization and back
              (2011) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Miranda-ActionAngleCoordinates.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy+of+physics"} philosophy of physics
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+Catren"}> Gabriel Catren
              ,
              %em Towards a Group-Theoretical Interpretation of Mechanics
              (
              %a{:href => "http://philsci-archive.pitt.edu/10116/"}> PhilSci Archive
              )
          %p
            On geometric quantization of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
          %ul
            %li
              José Luis Alonso, Carlos Bouthelier-Madre, Jesús Clemente-Gallardo, David Martínez-Crespo,
              %em Geometric flavours of Quantum Field theory on a Cauchy hypersurface. Part II: Methods of quantization and evolution
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.07953"}> arXiv:2402.07953
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Discussion of relation to other qusntization schemes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joshua+Lackman"}> Joshua Lackman
              ,
              %em Geometric Quantization Without Polarizations
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.01513"}> arXiv:2405.01513
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#holographic_quantization Holographic quantization
          %p
            The geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+via+the+A-model"} quantization via the A-model
            is discussed in
          %ul#GukovWitten08
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Branes and Quantization
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.0305"} arXiv:0809.0305
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1282054099"} euclid
          %p
            See also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            below, around (
            %a{:href => "#Hawkins"}> Hawkins
            ).
          %h3#quantization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Spin
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^{\mathbb{C}}
            \-Quantization
          %ul#Hochs08
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Hochs"}> Peter Hochs
              ,
              %em Quantisation commutes with reduction for cocompact Hamiltonian group actions
              2008 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ru.nl/~landsman/ThesisPeterHochs.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul#Paradan09
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Emile+Paradan"}> Paul-Emile Paradan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spin-quantization commutes with reduction
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.1067"} arXiv:0911.1067
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jsg/1350392491"} Euclid
          %p
            See the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+by+push-forward"} geometric quantization by push-forward
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            The basic example of geometric quantization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            is discussed in pretty much every text on the matter for instance
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Nohara"} Nohara, starting with example 2.6
          %p
            Discussion of geometric quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            is for instance in
          %ul#Witten
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              (lecture notes by Lisa Jeffrey),
              = succeed "," do
                %em New results in Chern-Simons theory
              %em Geometry of low dimensional manifolds 2: Symplectic manifolds and Jones-Witten theory
              (1989) (
              %a{:href => "http://cs5538.userapi.com/u11728334/docs/06f79688de6f/S_K_Donaldson_Geometry_of_LowDimensional_Ma.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul
            %li
              Scott Axelrod, Steve Della Pietra, and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization of Chern-Simons gauge theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214446565"} EUCLID
          %p
            Discussion of geometric quantization of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+varieties"} abelian varieties
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toric+varieties"} toric varieties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            and its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
            is in
          %ul#Nohara
            %li
              Yuichi Nohara,
              %em Independence of polarization in geometric quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://geoquant.mi.ras.ru/nohara.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul#Tyurin
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Tyurin"}> Andrei Tyurin
              ,
              %em Quantization, classical and quantum field theory and theta functions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0210466v1"}> arXiv:math/0210466v1
              )
          %ul
            %li
              N.J. Hitchin,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 131
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104200841"} euclid
          %p
            An appearance of geometric quantization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            is pointed out in
          %ul
            %li
              Andrei Tyurin,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization and mirror symmetry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9902027"} math.AG/9902027
          %p
            For discussion of the geometric quantization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "string#ReferencesSymplecticGeometryAndGeometricQuantization"} string – Symplectic geometry and geometric quantization
          %p
            Discussion of geometric quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Samuel Monnier,
              %em Geometric quantization and the metric dependence of the self-dual field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.5890"}> arXiv:1011.5890
              )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+theory"} Gromov-Witten theory
          %ul#CladerPriddisShoemaker13
            %li
              Emily Clader, Nathan Priddis, Mark Shoemaker,
              %em Geometric Quantization with Applications to Gromov-Witten Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1150"}> arXiv:1309.1150
              )
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToDeformation Relation to deformation quantization
          %p
            Discussion of the relation of geometric quantization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
              ,
              %em The Correspondence between Geometric Quantization and Formal Deformation Quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811049"}> arXiv:math/9811049
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
              ,
              %em Geometric Quantization of Vector Bundles
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9808116"}> arXiv:math/9808116
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Christoph Nölle,
              %em Geometric and deformation quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.5336"}> arXiv:0903.5336
              )
          %p For a basic comparative review of both see also section 1 of
          %ul#GukovWitten08
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Branes and Quantization
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.0305"} arXiv:0809.0305
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1282054099"} euclid
          %p
            (which then develops geometric
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+via+the+A-model"} quantization via the A-model
          %h3#relation_to_path_integral_quantization Relation to path integral quantization
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral+quantization"} path integral quantization
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Laurent Charles,
              %em Feynman path integral and Toeplitz Quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://ipht.cea.fr/DocsphtV2/articles/t98/093/public/publi.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#ReferencesBRST Geometric BRST quantization
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            version of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            is given (dually) by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
          %p Geometric quantization over BRST complexes is discussed in the following articles.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takashi+Kimura"}> Takashi Kimura
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BRST Quantization and Poisson Reduction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1990PhDT.......142K"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takashi+Kimura"} Takashi Kimura
                %em Geometric BRST quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/Research/PVBLICATIONS/gq.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                %em> Geometric BRST quantization. I. Prequantization
                , Comm. Math. Phys. Volume 136, Number 2 (1991), 209-229. (
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104202348"}> Euclid
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Tuynman"}> Gijs Tuynman
                ,
                %em Geometric quantization of the BRST charge
                Comm. Math. Phys. Volume 150, Number 2 (1992), 237-265. (
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104251864"}> Euclid
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.univ-lille1.fr/~gmt/PaperFolder/GQofBRST.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronald+Fulp"}> Ronald Fulp
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BRST Extension of Geometric Quantization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0604270"} arXiv:math/0604270
          %h3#ReferencesSupergeometric Supergeometric version
          %p
            One can consider geometric quantization in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                S.-M. Fei, H. -Y. Guo und Y. Yu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Symplectic geometry and geometric quantization on supermanifold with
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                    numbers
            %li
              %p
                Gijs M. Tuynman,
                %em Super Symplectic Geometry and Prequantization
                (2003) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0306049"}> arXiv:math-ph/0306049
                )
          %h3#of_presymplectic_manifolds Of presymplectic manifolds
          %p
            Discussion of quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+manifolds"} presymplectic manifolds
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                C. Günther,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Presymplectic manifolds and the quantization of relativistic particles
                %em , 383-400 (1979)
            %li
              %p
                Izu Vaisman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization on presymplectic manifolds
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ana+Canas+da+Silva"}> Ana Canas da Silva
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yael+Karshon"} Yael Karshon
                %em Quantization of Presymplectic Manifolds and Circle Actions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9705008"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9705008
                )
          %h3#of_generalized_complex_manifolds Of generalized complex manifolds
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Zambon"} Marco Zambon
                %em Variations on Prequantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412502"}> arXiv:math/0412502
                )
            %li
              %p
                Alexander Cardona,
                %em Geometric quantization of generalized complex manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://pentagono.uniandes.edu.co/~acardona/GQGCM.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %h3#in_higher_differential_geometry In higher differential geometry
          %p
            Geometric quantization in or with tools of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            is discussed in the following references.
          %ul
            %li#Bos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rogier+Bos"}> Rogier Bos
              ,
              %em Groupoids in geometric quantization
              PhD Thesis (2007)
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ist.utl.pt/~rbos/ProefschriftA4.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            is accomplished in
          %ul
            %li#Hawkins
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A groupoid approach to quantization
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.SG/0612363"} arXiv:math.SG/0612363
            %li#Nuiten13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
                , section 5.2.2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local boundary prequantum field theory
          %p
